    "original_query": "{'trace': {'query': 'How many edits were made to the Wikipedia page on Antidisestablishmentarianism from its inception until June of 2023?', 'messages': [{'step': 1, 'agent': 'WebServing_Expert', 'message': {'content': 'You are given: (1) a task and advises from your manager with a specific plan and (2) a general task.\\nCollect information from the general task, follow the suggestions from manager to solve the task.\\n\\n# General Task\\nHow many edits were made to the Wikipedia page on Antidisestablishmentarianism from its inception until June of 2023? Please solve the problem carefully.\\n\\n# Task and suggestions from manager\\n## Task description\\nDetermine the number of edits made to the Wikipedia page on Antidisestablishmentarianism from its inception until June of 2023.\\n\\n## Plan for solving the task\\n1. Obtain a Valid Wikimedia API Token: Follow the instructions provided to obtain a valid API token.\\n2. Re-execute the API Call: Use the valid token to fetch the edit history of the page.\\n3. Filter the Edits: Filter the edits to include only those made until June 2023.\\n4. Count the Edits: Count the number of filtered edits.\\n\\n## Output format\\nThe output should be a single integer representing the number of edits made to the Wikipedia page on Antidisestablishmentarianism from its inception until June 2023.\\n\\n## Constraints and conditions for completion\\n- Ensure that the data is accurate and up-to-date as of June 2023.\\n- The count should include all types of edits (minor, major, etc.).\\n- The solution should handle any potential API rate limits or restrictions.\\n\\n## Results from last response\\n0 edits were found for the Wikipedia page on Antidisestablishmentarianism until June 2023 due to an authentication error (`401 Unauthorized`).\\n\\n## Updated Code with Enhanced Debugging\\n```python\\nimport requests\\nimport json\\n\\ndef get_page_edits(title, start_date, end_date, token):\\n    url = f\\'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/api.php\\'\\n    params = {\\n        \\'action\\': \\'query\\',\\n        \\'format\\': \\'json\\',\\n        \\'prop\\': \\'revisions\\',\\n        \\'titles\\': title,\\n        \\'rvlimit\\': \\'max\\',\\n        \\'rvstart\\': start_date,\\n        \\'rvend\\': end_date\\n    }\\n    headers = {\\n        \\'Authorization\\': f\\'Bearer {token}\\'\\n    }\\n\\n    response = requests.get(url, headers=headers, params=params)\\n    \\n    # Debugging: Print the status code, response headers, and response content to understand the issue\\n    print(f\\'Status Code: {response.status_code}\\')\\n    print(f\\'Response Headers: {response.headers}\\')\\n    print(f\\'Response Content: {response.text}\\')\\n    \\n    data = response.json()\\n\\n    if \\'query\\' not in data:\\n        raise ValueError(\"API response does not contain \\'query\\' key. Please check the API request and token.\")\\n\\n    page_id = list(data[\\'query\\'][\\'pages\\'].keys())[0]\\n    revisions = data[\\'query\\'][\\'pages\\'][page_id].get(\\'revisions\\', [])\\n\\n    return len(revisions)\\n\\ndef main():\\n    title = \\'Antidisestablishmentarianism\\'\\n    start_date = \\'2001-01-01T00:00:00Z\\'\\n    end_date = \\'2023-06-30T23:59:59Z\\'\\n    token = \\'YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN\\'  # Replace this with your actual API token\\n\\n    total_edits = 0\\n    more_edits = True\\n    while more_edits:\\n        count = get_page_edits(title, start_date, end_date, token)\\n        total_edits += count\\n        more_edits = count == 500  # If 500 edits are fetched, there might be more\\n\\n    print(f\\'Total edits made to the Wikipedia page on {title} until June 2023: {total_edits}\\')\\n\\nif __name__ == \\'__main__\\':\\n    main()\\n``` ', 'name': 'WebServing_Expert', 'role': 'assistant'}}, {'step': 2, 'agent': 'WebServing_Expert', 'message': {'content': 'Address: bing: how to obtain a valid Wikimedia API token\\nTitle: how to obtain a valid Wikimedia API token - Search\\nViewport position: Showing page 1 of 1.\\n=======================\\nA Bing search for \\'how to obtain a valid Wikimedia API token\\' found 10 results:\\n\\n## Web Results\\n1. [Managing API keys - API Portal - Wikimedia](https://api.wikimedia.org/wiki/Managing_API_keys)\\nThe API keys dashboard lets you create and manage OAuth 2.0 credentials for use with the Wikimedia API.. Create a key. To create an API key, select Create key, and complete the registration form.. Create app credentials. App credentials let you build an app to publish and share. Wikimedia API requests are rate limited based on client ID, so you should create one set of credentials per app.\\n\\n2. [Getting started with Wikimedia APIs - API Portal](https://api.wikimedia.org/wiki/Getting_started_with_Wikimedia_APIs)\\nSelect Create key, and select the Personal API token option. This token is tied to your account. It should only be used by you and should not be published or shared. Remember to store your token in a secure place, like a password manager. ... The Wikimedia API uses OAuth 2.0 for authentication and authorization. Create an API key to get started ...\\n\\n3. [Authentication - API Portal - Wikimedia](https://api.wikimedia.org/wiki/Authentication)\\nApps using the Wikimedia API should authenticate their requests using OAuth 2.0.This provides a secure process for accessing Wikimedia resources and applies an app-specific rate limit.For a streamlined experience for evaluation and prototyping, you can authenticate using a personal API token.. App authentication: OAuth 2.0 client credentials flow; User authentication: OAuth 2.0 authorization ...\\n\\n4. [dart - Wikimedia CSRF Token invalid - Stack Overflow](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/69480938/wikimedia-csrf-token-invalid)\\nI am using the MediaWiki Action API, where I use the OAuth2 authorization flow to obtain a access token. For uploading a image, a CSRF Token is required. I get the token by making a post request to...\\n\\n5. [API:Tutorial - MediaWiki](https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/API:Tutorial)\\nThe Action API is available for third-party developers, Wikimedia extension developers, and wiki site administrators. On the right sidebar of this page, there are many features that are supported by the API, grouped by category. ... You would need to obtain tokens via API:Tokens to proceed further. Resources. Use Special:APISandbox to ...\\n\\n6. [Wikidata : REST API/Authentication](https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Wikidata:REST_API/Authentication)\\nHere’s a quick overview of what you need to know to get authenticated and authorized when using the Wikibase REST API on Wikidata: Set up OAuth 2.0 for your API access on meta.wikimedia.org, Wikimedia\\'s central OAuth service; Use your new credentials to start using the API; Learn how to properly interact with the Wikibase REST API when ...\\n\\n7. [Wikipedia API - Public APIs](https://publicapis.io/wikipedia-api)\\nTo use the MediaWiki API, you need to authenticate yourself by obtaining an API token. This token is used to identify your API requests and ensure that only authorized clients can access the API. To obtain an API token, you need to have an account on one of the Wikimedia projects.\\n\\n8. [Documentation/Getting started/Managing API keys - API Portal - Wikimedia](https://api.wikimedia.org/wiki/Documentation/Getting_started/Managing_API_keys)\\nThe Wikimedia Foundation, Inc is a nonprofit charitable organization dedicated to encouraging the growth, development and distribution of free, multilingual content, and to providing the full content of these wiki-based projects to the public free of charge.\\n\\n9. [How to set an authorization bearer token in Postman?](https://www.indiehackers.com/post/how-to-set-an-authorization-bearer-token-in-postman-0a0a2afef8)\\nStep 1:Obtain the Bearer Token. To begin, acquire a valid bearer token that contains essential information such as user ID, permissions, and expiry details. ... Click on the \"Send\" button to validate the token with the API server. The server will decode the header, extract the token, validate it, and authenticate the request if the token is ...\\n\\n10. [API:REST API - MediaWiki](https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/API:REST_API)\\nDesigned to provide long-term stability for developers, the MediaWiki REST API is versioned using a global version number in the API path (for example: /v1/).Following the principles of semantic versioning, the version is incremented when an endpoint is changed in a backwards-incompatible way, such as removing a response property or adding a required parameter.', 'name': 'WebServing_Expert', 'role': 'assistant'}}, {'step': 3, 'agent': 'WebServing_Expert', 'message': {'content': 'Address: https://api.wikimedia.org/wiki/Managing_API_keys\\nTitle: Managing API keys - API Portal\\nViewport position: Showing page 1 of 2.\\n=======================\\nManaging API keys - API Portal\\n\\n[Jump to content](#content)\\n\\n[Wikimedia\\nAPI Portal](/wiki/Main_Page \"Visit the main page\")\\n\\n[Learn](/wiki/Learn)\\n[API catalog](/wiki/API_catalog)\\n[Maintainers](/wiki/Maintainers)\\n[Community](/wiki/Community)\\n\\n[Log in](/w/index.php?title=Special:UserLogin&returnto=Managing+API+keys)\\n\\n[Jump to content](#content)\\n\\n[Learn](/wiki/Learn)\\n[API catalog](/wiki/API_catalog)\\n[Maintainers](/wiki/Maintainers)\\n[Community](/wiki/Community)\\n\\n[Wikimedia\\nAPI Portal](/wiki/Main_Page \"Visit the main page\")\\n\\n[Log in](/w/index.php?title=Special:UserLogin&returnto=Managing+API+keys)\\n\\nManaging API keys\\n=================\\n\\n[Discussion](/wiki/Talk:Managing_API_keys)\\n[Updated 11 July 2023](/w/index.php?title=Managing_API_keys&action=history)\\n \\n\\nThe [API keys dashboard](/wiki/Special:AppManagement \"Special:AppManagement\") lets you create and manage OAuth 2.0 credentials for use with the Wikimedia API.\\n\\nCreate a key\\n------------\\n\\nTo create an API key, select **Create key**, and complete the registration form.\\n\\n### Create app credentials\\n\\nApp credentials let you build an app to publish and share. Wikimedia API requests are rate limited based on client ID, so you should create one set of credentials per app. To create credentials, select an app type, and provide a redirect URL.\\n\\n* **Name**: Choose a unique name to help identify your app.\\n* **Description**: Admins use this field to evaluate your client, so include a description of how your app uses Wikimedia content.\\n* **Redirect URI** is used by the OAuth authentication server to return users to your app after approval.\\n\\nApp credentials with edit permissions must be approved by Wikimedia OAuth administrators before they can be used. You can see the status of your client on the [API keys dashboard](/wiki/Special:AppManagement \"Special:AppManagement\"). Once your app is approved, you\\'ll receive an email from wiki@wikimedia.org.\\n\\n### Create a personal API token\\n\\nA personal API token is tied to your Wikimedia account. It should only be used by you and should not be published or shared. To create a personal API token, select the **API token** key type. After submitting the form, you\\'ll be shown a client ID, client secret, and access token. Remember to store your access token in a secure place; you won\\'t be able to access it again through the API Portal. Personal API tokens are approved automatically.\\n\\nKey status\\n----------\\n\\nThe [API keys dashboard](/wiki/Special:AppManagement \"Special:AppManagement\") displays the status of each key.\\n\\n* **Approved** keys are ready to use.\\n* **Approval pending** keys are waiting for review and approval by Wikimedia OAuth admins. Approval usually occurs within two weeks.\\n* **Rejected** keys have been rejected by Wikimedia OAuth admins. This is usually due to security concerns or missing or unclear information. If your key is rejected, you should receive an email from wiki@wikimedia.org with the rejection reason and steps to re-submit your key.\\n* **Expired** keys have not been approved within 30 days. If your key is expired, please re-create the key.\\n* **Disabled** keys have been disabled by Wikimedia OAuth admins due to security concerns or risky behavior.\\n\\nReset secrets\\n-------------\\n\\nTo reset a client secret, select **View details** for the key on the [API keys dashboard](/wiki/Special:AppManagement \"Special:AppManagement\"), and select **Reset client secret**. This resets all provided secrets for the key, including a personal API token. Resetting a secret does not invalidate existing secrets.\\n\\n  \\n\\n  \\n\\n![](https://login.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:CentralAutoLogin/start?useformat=desktop&type=1x1&usesul3=0)\\nRetrieved from \"<https://api.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Managing_API_keys&oldid=1865>\"\\n\\nThe Wikimedia Foundation, Inc is a nonprofit charitable organization dedicated to encouraging the growth, development and distribution of free, multilingual content, and to providing the full content of these wiki-based projects to the public free of charge.\\n\\n[Contact](https://wikimediafoundation.org/about/contact/)\\n[About Wikimedia](https://wikimediafoundation.org/about/)\\n\\n### Wikimedia Projects\\n\\n[Wikipedia](https://www.wikipedia.org/)[Wikibooks](https://www.wikibooks.org/)[Wikiversity](https://www.wikiversity.org/)[Wikinews](https://www.wikinews.org/)[Wiktionary](https://www.wiktionary.org/)[Wikisource](https://www.wikisource.org/)[Wikiquote](https://www.wikiquote.org/)[Wikivoyage](https://www.wikivoyage.org/)[Wikimedia Commons](https://commons.wikimedia.org/)[Wikidata](https://www.wikidata.org/)[Wikispecies](https://species.wikimedia.org/)[MediaWiki](https://www.mediawiki.org/)\\n\\n### Movement affiliates\\n\\n[Wikimedia Chapters](https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Wikimedia_chapters)[Wikimedia Thematic Organizations](https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Wikimedia_thematic_organizations)[Wikimedia User Groups](https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Wikimedia_user_groups)\\n\\n### OTHER\\n\\n[Terms of use](https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:MyLanguage/Policy:Terms_of_Use)[Privacy policy](https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:MyLanguage/Policy:Privacy_policy)[Disclaimers](https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:MyLanguage/Policy:General_disclaimer)[Accessibility ', 'name': 'WebServing_Expert', 'role': 'assistant'}}, {'step': 4, 'agent': 'WebServing_Expert', 'message': {'content': 'To obtain a valid Wikimedia API token, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Log in to the Wikimedia API Portal**: If you don\\'t have an account, create one.\\n\\n2. **Create a Key**:\\n   - Navigate to the [API keys dashboard](https://api.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:AppManagement).\\n   - Select \"Create key\" and complete the registration form.\\n\\n3. **Choose the Key Type**:\\n   - For a personal use API token, select the **API token** key type.\\n   - For app credentials, select the app type, provide a redirect URL, and include a description of your app.\\n\\n4. **Get Your Credentials**:\\n   - After submitting the form, you will receive a client ID, client secret, and access token.\\n   - Store your access token securely, as you will not be able to access it again through the API Portal.\\n\\nOnce you have obtained your API token, you can use it to authenticate your requests to the Wikimedia API.', 'name': 'WebServing_Expert', 'role': 'assistant'}}, {'step': 5, 'agent': 'Computer_terminal', 'message': {'content': 'There is no code from the last 1 message for me to execute. Group chat manager should let other participants to continue the conversation. If the group chat manager want to end the conversation, you should let other participant reply me only with \"TERMINATE\"', 'name': 'Computer_terminal', 'role': 'user'}}, {'step': 6, 'agent': 'Verification_Expert', 'message': {'content': 'Now that you have obtained your Wikimedia API token, update the code with your valid token and re-execute the API call to fetch the edit history of the Wikipedia page on Antidisestablishmentarianism.\\n\\nHere is the updated Python code:\\n\\n```python\\nimport requests\\nimport json\\n\\ndef get_page_edits(title, start_date, end_date, token):\\n    url = f\\'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/api.php\\'\\n    params = {\\n        \\'action\\': \\'query\\',\\n        \\'format\\': \\'json\\',\\n        \\'prop\\': \\'revisions\\',\\n        \\'titles\\': title,\\n        \\'rvlimit\\': \\'max\\',\\n        \\'rvstart\\': start_date,\\n        \\'rvend\\': end_date\\n    }\\n    headers = {\\n        \\'Authorization\\': f\\'Bearer {token}\\'\\n    }\\n\\n    response = requests.get(url, headers=headers, params=params)\\n    \\n    # Debugging: Print the status code, response headers, and response content to understand the issue\\n    print(f\\'Status Code: {response.status_code}\\')\\n    print(f\\'Response Headers: {response.headers}\\')\\n    print(f\\'Response Content: {response.text}\\')\\n    \\n    data = response.json()\\n\\n    if \\'query\\' not in data:\\n        raise ValueError(\"API response does not contain \\'query\\' key. Please check the API request and token.\")\\n\\n    page_id = list(data[\\'query\\'][\\'pages\\'].keys())[0]\\n    revisions = data[\\'query\\'][\\'pages\\'][page_id].get(\\'revisions\\', [])\\n\\n    return len(revisions)\\n\\ndef main():\\n    title = \\'Antidisestablishmentarianism\\'\\n    start_date = \\'2001-01-01T00:00:00Z\\'\\n    end_date = \\'2023-06-30T23:59:59Z\\'\\n    token = \\'YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN\\'  # Replace this with your actual API token\\n\\n    total_edits = 0\\n    more_edits = True\\n    while more_edits:\\n        count = get_page_edits(title, start_date, end_date, token)\\n        total_edits += count\\n        more_edits = count == 500  # If 500 edits are fetched, there might be more\\n\\n    print(f\\'Total edits made to the Wikipedia page on {title} until June 2023: {total_edits}\\')\\n\\nif __name__ == \\'__main__\\':\\n    main()\\n```\\n\\nReplace `\\'YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN\\'` with your actual API token and run the code again. This should give you the number of edits made to the Wikipedia page on Antidisestablishmentarianism from its inception until June 2023. Once the result is obtained, please share it for verification.', 'name': 'Verification_Expert', 'role': 'user'}}, {'step': 7, 'agent': 'Computer_terminal', 'message': {'content': 'exitcode: 1 (execution failed)\\nCode output: Traceback (most recent call last):\\n  File \"/home/CaptainAgent/groupchat/tmp_code_73ca303802da6c2857c3682499f347fc.py\", line 52, in <module>\\n    main()\\n  File \"/home/CaptainAgent/groupchat/tmp_code_73ca303802da6c2857c3682499f347fc.py\", line 45, in main\\n    count = get_page_edits(title, start_date, end_date, token)\\n  File \"/home/CaptainAgent/groupchat/tmp_code_73ca303802da6c2857c3682499f347fc.py\", line 29, in get_page_edits\\n    raise ValueError(\"API response does not contain \\'query\\' key. Please check the API request and token.\")\\nValueError: API response does not contain \\'query\\' key. Please check the API request and token.\\nStatus Code: 200\\nResponse Headers: {\\'date\\': \\'Thu, 19 Dec 2024 18:29:01 GMT\\', \\'server\\': \\'mw-api-ext.eqiad.main-5b9f7b6d97-hf8zf\\', \\'x-content-type-options\\': \\'nosniff\\', \\'mediawiki-api-error\\': \\'mwoauth-invalid-authorization\\', \\'x-frame-options\\': \\'DENY\\', \\'content-disposition\\': \\'inline; filename=api-result.json\\', \\'cache-control\\': \\'private, must-revalidate, max-age=0\\', \\'vary\\': \\'Accept-Encoding\\', \\'content-type\\': \\'application/json; charset=utf-8\\', \\'content-encoding\\': \\'gzip\\', \\'age\\': \\'0\\', \\'x-cache\\': \\'cp1114 pass, cp1114 pass\\', \\'x-cache-status\\': \\'pass\\', \\'server-timing\\': \\'cache;desc=\"pass\", host;desc=\"cp1114\"\\', \\'strict-transport-security\\': \\'max-age=106384710; includeSubDomains; preload\\', \\'report-to\\': \\'{ \"group\": \"wm_nel\", \"max_age\": 604800, \"endpoints\": [{ \"url\": \"https://intake-logging.wikimedia.org/v1/events?stream=w3c.reportingapi.network_error&schema_uri=/w3c/reportingapi/network_error/1.0.0\" }] }\\', \\'nel\\': \\'{ \"report_to\": \"wm_nel\", \"max_age\": 604800, \"failure_fraction\": 0.05, \"success_fraction\": 0.0}\\', \\'set-cookie\\': \\'WMF-Last-Access=19-Dec-2024;Path=/;HttpOnly;secure;Expires=Mon, 20 Jan 2025 12:00:00 GMT, WMF-Last-Access-Global=19-Dec-2024;Path=/;Domain=.wikipedia.org;HttpOnly;secure;Expires=Mon, 20 Jan 2025 12:00:00 GMT, GeoIP=US:NC:Durham:35.96:-78.93:v4; Path=/; secure; Domain=.wikipedia.org, NetworkProbeLimit=0.001;Path=/;Secure;SameSite=Lax;Max-Age=3600\\', \\'x-client-ip\\': \\'152.3.34.5\\', \\'accept-ranges\\': \\'bytes\\', \\'transfer-encoding\\': \\'chunked\\'}\\nResponse Content: {\"error\":{\"code\":\"mwoauth-invalid-authorization\",\"info\":\"The authorization headers in your request are not valid: Invalid access token\",\"*\":\"See https://en.wikipedia.org/w/api.php for API usage. Subscribe to the mediawiki-api-announce mailing list at &lt;https://lists.wikimedia.org/postorius/lists/mediawiki-api-announce.lists.wikimedia.org/&gt; for notice of API deprecations and breaking changes.\"},\"servedby\":\"mw-api-ext.eqiad.main-5b9f7b6d97-hf8zf\"}\\n', 'name': 'Computer_terminal', 'role': 'user'}}, {'step': 8, 'agent': 'WebServing_Expert', 'message': {'content': 'Address: bing: number of edits to Wikipedia page on Antidisestablishmentarianism from inception to June 2023\\nTitle: number of edits to Wikipedia page on Antidisestablishmentarianism from inception to June 2023 - Search\\nViewport position: Showing page 1 of 1.\\n=======================\\nA Bing search for \\'number of edits to Wikipedia page on Antidisestablishmentarianism from inception to June 2023\\' found 10 results:\\n\\n## Web Results\\n1. [Wikipedia:List of Wikipedians by number of edits - Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:List_of_Wikipedians_by_number_of_edits)\\nThis is a list of Wikipedians ordered by number of edits in the English-language Wikipedia.Edits performed by Wikipedians in all namespaces (articles, talk pages, user page, user talk, templates, files etc.) are counted.Some types of edits that may be included in certain page count tools, such as page moves, are not captured by the counting method employed to compile this list, so there may be ...\\n\\n2. [Antidisestablishmentarianism - Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antidisestablishmentarianism)\\nArms of the See of Canterbury, governing the Church of England. Antidisestablishmentarianism (/ ˌ æ n t i d ɪ s ɪ ˌ s t æ b l ɪ ʃ m ə n ˈ t ɛər i ə n ɪ z əm / ⓘ, US also / ˌ æ n t aɪ-/ ⓘ) is a position that advocates that a state church (the \"established church\") should continue to receive government patronage, rather than be disestablished (i.e., be separated from the ...\\n\\n3. [Wikipedia:Time Between Edits - Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Time_Between_Edits)\\nThe current number of edits is 1,258,882,722 Graph 2005–2020 This graph shows the time taken for every ten millionth edit between July 31, 2005, and May 31, 2020. ... 21:51, 13 June 2023: 59 days 8 weeks 1,170,000,000 17:47 12 August 2023: 60 days 9 weeks 1,180,000,000 21:57, 13 October 2023: 62 days 9 weeks 1,190,000,000 09:04, 15 December ...\\n\\n4. [Wikipedia Statistics - Tables - Edits per month - Wikimedia](https://stats.wikimedia.org/EN/TablesDatabaseEdits.htm)\\nWikipedia Statistics: Show Firefox: ... Edits per month: Edits in past month (incl. redirects, incl. unregistered contributors, incl. bots) Jan 31, 2019: This is the final release of Wikistats-1 dump-based reports. Part of these data are available in the first release of Wikistats 2.\\n\\n5. [21+ Wikipedia Statistics to Keep You Updated in 2023 - Leftronic](https://leftronic.com/blog/wikipedia-statistics)\\nWikipedia receives 825 million edits on 39 million pages of content. The most viewed page on Wikipedia is the main page. The size of Wikipedia is about 200 terabytes. The Catalan Wikipedia was among the first non-English ones to be added. Wikipedia has experienced 1 billion edits from about 27 million users across 17.6 million articles.\\n\\n6. [The Most Edited Wikipedia Pages - Rouge Media](https://www.rouge-media.com/insights/the-most-edited-wikipedia-pages/)\\nThe themes above include both high-profile pages and more obscure topics. It’s clear that being the definitive source of information on the internet requires a lot of upkeep. Despite this, the number of editors has fallen over the last 15 years. In 2011, Wikipedia set itself a target to reach 200,000 active editors by 2015.\\n\\n7. [The Most Edited Wikipedia Articles Of The Last Decade](https://www.statista.com/chart/4252/the-most-edited-wikipedia-articles-of-the-last-decade/)\\nGeorge W. Bush is the Wikipedia page with the most edits of all time, some 46,000. It is also the most edited entry in a single year with people tweaking it 20,894 times in 2005.\\n\\n8. [Wikipedia API: how to get the number of revisions of a page?](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/7136343/wikipedia-api-how-to-get-the-number-of-revisions-of-a-page)\\nAnyone know how to get the number of revisions of a wikipedia page using mediawiki API? I have read this API documentation, but can\\'t find the related API: Revision API ... 2023 at 19:57. answered Oct 21, 2023 at 19:40. ... How to get total number of edits for a given wikipedia page from the API? 1.\\n\\n9. [What is in an edit? Automated detection of edit types on Wikipedia](https://techblog.wikimedia.org/2022/06/28/what-is-in-an-edit-automated-detection-of-edit-types-on-wikipedia/)\\nOur goal with this project was to generate diffs that provided a structured summary of the what of an edit – in effect seeking to replicate what many editors naturally do when viewing diffs on Wikipedia or the auto-generated edit summaries on Wikidata . For the edit to Lady Cockburn, that might look like: 1 template insert, 1 template change ...\\n\\n10. [Antidisestablishmentarianism (word) - Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antidisestablishmentarianism_(word))\\nThe English word antidisestablishmentarianism (UK / ˌ æ n t i d ɪ s ɪ ˌ s t æ b l ɪ ʃ m ə n ˈ t ɛər i ə n ɪ z əm / ⓘ US / ˌ æ n t aɪ-/ ⓘ) is notable for its unusual length of 28 letters and 12 syllables, and is one of the longest words in the English language. [1] It has been cited as the longest word in the English language (excluding coined and technical terms ...', 'name': 'WebServing_Expert', 'role': 'assistant'}}, {'step': 9, 'agent': 'WebServing_Expert', 'message': {'content': 'Address: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antidisestablishmentarianism\\nTitle: Antidisestablishmentarianism - Wikipedia\\nViewport position: Showing page 1 of 3.\\n=======================\\n# Antidisestablishmentarianism\\n\\nPolitical movement in the UK[![](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Angl-Canterbury-Arms.svg/200px-Angl-Canterbury-Arms.svg.png)](/wiki/File:Angl-Canterbury-Arms.svg)\\n\\nArms of the [See of Canterbury](/wiki/See_of_Canterbury \"See of Canterbury\"), governing the [Church of England](/wiki/Church_of_England \"Church of England\")\\n\\n**Antidisestablishmentarianism** ([/ˌæntidɪsɪˌstæblɪʃmənˈtɛəriənɪzəm/](/wiki/Help:IPA/English \"Help:IPA/English\") [ⓘ](/wiki/File:Antidisestablishmentarianism.ogg \"File:Antidisestablishmentarianism.ogg\"), US also [/ˌæntaɪ-/](/wiki/Help:IPA/English \"Help:IPA/English\") [ⓘ](/wiki/File:Pronunciation_of_%27antidisestablishmentarianism%27.ogg \"File:Pronunciation of \\'antidisestablishmentarianism\\'.ogg\")) is a position that advocates that a [state church](/wiki/State_Church \"State Church\") (the \"established church\") should continue to receive government patronage, rather than be disestablished (i.e., be separated from the state).[[1]](#cite_note-Findley2017-1)[[2]](#cite_note-2)\\n\\nIn 19th century Britain, it developed as a political movement in opposition to [disestablishmentarianism](/wiki/Disestablishmentarianism \"Disestablishmentarianism\"), the [Liberal Party](/wiki/Liberal_Party_(UK) \"Liberal Party (UK)\")\\'s efforts to [disestablish](/wiki/Disestablishment \"Disestablishment\") or remove the [Church of England](/wiki/Church_of_England \"Church of England\") as the [official state church](/wiki/State_Church \"State Church\") of England, [Ireland](/wiki/Ireland \"Ireland\"), and [Wales](/wiki/Wales \"Wales\"). The Church\\'s status has been maintained in England, but in Ireland, [the Anglican Church of Ireland](/wiki/Church_of_Ireland \"Church of Ireland\") was disestablished in 1871. In Wales, four Church of England [dioceses](/wiki/Diocese \"Diocese\") were disestablished in 1920 and became the [Church in Wales](/wiki/Church_in_Wales \"Church in Wales\"). In colonial America, the Church of England was disestablished in six colonies despite its mild popularity in the 1780s; many Anglicans in America began to refer to themselves as [Episcopalians](/wiki/Episcopal_Church_(United_States) \"Episcopal Church (United States)\").[[3]](#cite_note-3)\\n\\n*Antidisestablishmentarianism* is also frequently noted as one of the [longest non-scientific words](/wiki/Antidisestablishmentarianism_(word) \"Antidisestablishmentarianism (word)\") in the English language.\\n\\nHistory\\n-------\\n\\n[[edit](/w/index.php?title=Antidisestablishmentarianism&action=edit&section=1 \"Edit section: History\")]\\n\\nThe matter of disestablishment of the Church of England is an ongoing issue, often tied with the position of the [Monarchy of the United Kingdom](/wiki/English_monarch \"English monarch\") as [\"Supreme Governor\" of the Church](/wiki/Supreme_Governor_of_the_Church_of_England \"Supreme Governor of the Church of England\") (see [Act of Settlement 1701](/wiki/Act_of_Settlement_1701 \"Act of Settlement 1701\")).\\n\\nBritish philosopher [Phillip Blond](/wiki/Phillip_Blond \"Phillip Blond\"), an advocate of the antidisestablishmentarian position, argues that England\\'s having a state church has prevented the country from embracing any sort of ethnic or racial nationalism.[[4]](#cite_note-Blond2010-4) Blond has stated that official patronage of the [Church of England](/wiki/Church_of_England \"Church of England\") has allowed the country to withstand and speak against totalitarian ideologies of the 20th century that were plaguing other parts of the world.[[4]](#cite_note-Blond2010-4) He further opined that \"Just as we need the church to protect the political, so we need it to protect the idea of civil society.\"[[4]](#cite_note-Blond2010-4) Blond concludes that the \"church establishment in England creates a more diverse political and social life, prevents religious extremism and helps to minimise partisan conflict and secular violence.\"[[4]](#cite_note-Blond2010-4) [Giles Coren](/wiki/Giles_Coren \"Giles Coren\"), a British writer, supports antidisestablishmentarianism because it allows all English people to receive meaningful [rites](/wiki/Rite_(Christianity) \"Rite (Christianity)\") such as marriage.[[5]](#cite_note-Corren2012-5)\\n\\nIn April 2014, [Nick Clegg](/wiki/Nick_Clegg \"Nick Clegg\"), then [Deputy Prime Minister of the United Kingdom](/wiki/Deputy_Prime_Minister_of_the_United_Kingdom \"Deputy Prime Minister of the United Kingdom\") and [Leader of the Liberal Democrats](/wiki/Leader_of_the_Liberal_Democrats \"Leader of the Liberal Democrats\"), said that he thought the Church of England and the British state should be separated \"in the long run\".[[6]](#cite_note-clegg-6) [David Cameron](/wiki/David_Cameron \"David Cameron\"), the [Prime Minister of the United Kingdom](/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_the_United_Kingdom \"Prime Minister of the United Kingdom\") at the time, responded to Clegg\\'s comments by stating that the position was \"a long-term Liberal idea, but it is not a [Conservative](/wiki/Conservative_Party_(UK) \"Conservative Party (UK)\") one\", adding that he believed the existence of an established church is beneficial.[[6]](#cite_note-clegg-6)\\n\\nWord ', 'name': 'WebServing_Expert', 'role': 'assistant'}}, {'step': 10, 'agent': 'WebServing_Expert', 'message': {'content': 'Antidisestablishmentarianism is a political movement in the UK advocating for the continued government patronage of a state church, specifically opposing the separation of the Church of England from the state. This movement emerged in the 19th century in response to the Liberal Party\\'s disestablishmentarian efforts to remove the Church of England\\'s status as the official state church in England, Ireland, and Wales. While the Church\\'s status was preserved in England, the Anglican Church of Ireland was disestablished in 1871 and the Church in Wales in 1920. Proponents like philosopher Phillip Blond argue that an established church has helped England resist nationalism and totalitarian ideologies, thus promoting a more diverse political and social life, while reducing religious extremism and secular violence.\\n\\nThe term \"antidisestablishmentarianism\" is often noted for its length, being one of the longest non-scientific words in the English language, consisting of 28 letters and 12 syllables. Despite its recognition in the Oxford dictionary, it is not listed in Merriam-Webster\\'s dictionary of American English. The debate over the Church of England\\'s establishment continues, with figures like Nick Clegg advocating for separation, while others, such as former Prime Minister David Cameron, believe in the benefits of maintaining the established church.', 'name': 'WebServing_Expert', 'role': 'assistant'}}]}, 'prepared_observations': [{'facts': [{'fact': 'The task is to determine the number of edits made to a Wikipedia page, with a previous attempt failing due to an authentication error (401 Unauthorized).', 'step': 1}, {'fact': 'The WebServing_Expert provided instructions on how to obtain a valid Wikimedia API token.', 'step': 4}, {'fact': \"The code execution failed with a ValueError indicating th